Join the hunt — Kalikkam Zombies (Field Map Doodle style)
1080×1920, 30 fps, 31.1 s. Music and sound effects only; no voice, no subtitles.

Imagery
- Everything on screen is SVG drawn by code in kit.js, cast.js, screens.js and film.js. No photos, no
  generated images, no stock, no sprites.
- The zombie and survivor characters, the "Z⊕MBIES" wordmark, the phone screens (splash, tour, sign-in,
  Home) and the cream contour-line ground are the Kalikkam app's own designs (apps/web: Mascot.tsx,
  Welcome.tsx, Scenes.tsx, public/topo.svg), redrawn here in vector. topo.svg is the app's code-generated
  contour pattern, copied unchanged.
- The QR on the "Scan to infect" card is a real QR code for the text "Kalikkam vest", generated once with
  the qrcode package (npm, MIT licence) and baked into qr.js as path data.
- The phone is a generic rounded-rectangle bezel drawn in code; it imitates no real handset or brand.

Fonts
- Archivo (variable, wdth axis), Copyright 2020 The Archivo Project Authors
  (https://github.com/Omnibus-Type/Archivo). SIL Open Font License 1.1, full text in fonts/OFL-Archivo.txt.
  fonts/archivo-latin-wdth.woff2 is the Latin subset of the Google Fonts release, the same font the app uses.

Music and sound
- Original score and every sound effect synthesized in numpy/scipy by score.py: kick, clap, hats, snare,
  bass, marimba, bell, pad, crash, and foley (sonar ping, two-tone lock, tap, card slide, typing tick, pop,
  boing, riser, wind). Placed from the picture's own events (out/events.json). No samples, no third-party
  music.
- score.py imports helpers (filters, noise, heartbeat, whoosh, thump, ding) from the Lemo-Opuscar library,
  core/audio/sfx.py, under the MIT licence below.
- Techniques (not code) from the library's Game Show Flat style: tempo grid, event-driven score, back-ease
  pops; and from Living Screencast: push-in to the tap, pull back.

Software
- Lemo-Opuscar render tools (core/render: events.mjs, video.mjs, readcheck.mjs, mux.sh), MIT licence below.
- Playwright-core 1.63 (Apache-2.0) driving Chrome Headless Shell; FFmpeg 8.0.1 (libx264, AAC);
  Python 3 with numpy 2.5, scipy 1.18 and soundfile 0.14.

